{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PRO",
  "chapter": 29,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PRO.29.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.29.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He, that being often reproved hardeneth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " neck, shall suddenly be destroyed, and that without remedy.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.29.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.29.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When the righteous are in authority, the people rejoice: but when the wicked beareth rule, the people mourn.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.29.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.29.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that loveth wisdom rejoiceth his father: but he that keepeth company with harlots spendeth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " substance.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.29.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.29.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The king by judgment establisheth the land: but he that receiveth gifts overthroweth it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.29.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.29.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A man that flattereth his neighbor spreadeth a net for his feet.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.29.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.29.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In the transgression of an evil man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a snare: but the righteous doth sing and rejoice.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.29.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.29.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The righteous considereth the cause of the poor: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the wicked regardeth not to know ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.29.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.29.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Scornful men bring a city into a snare: but wise ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " turn away wrath.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.29.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.29.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a wise man contendeth with a foolish man, whether he rageth or laugheth, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no rest.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.29.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.29.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The blood-thirsty hate the upright: but the just seek his soul.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.29.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.29.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A fool uttereth all his mind: but a wise ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " keepeth it in till afterwards.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.29.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.29.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If a ruler hearkeneth to lies, all his servants ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wicked.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.29.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.29.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The poor and the deceitful man meet together: the LORD enlighteneth both their eyes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.29.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.29.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The king that faithfully judgeth the poor, his throne shall be established for ever.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.29.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.29.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The rod and reproof give wisdom: but a child left ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to himself",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bringeth his mother to shame.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.29.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.29.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When the wicked are multiplied, transgression increaseth: but the righteous shall see their fall.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.29.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.29.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Correct thy son, and he shall give thee rest; yes, he shall give delight to thy soul.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.29.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.29.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Where ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no vision, the people perish: but he that keepeth the law, happy ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.29.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.29.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A servant will not be corrected by words: for though he understandeth, he will not answer.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.29.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.29.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Seest thou a man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hasty in his words? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " more hope of a fool than of him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.29.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.29.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that delicately bringeth up his servant from a child shall have him at length become ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " son.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.29.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.29.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "An angry man stirreth up strife, and a furious man aboundeth in transgression.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.29.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.29.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A man's pride shall bring him low: but honor shall uphold the humble in spirit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.29.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.29.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whoever is partner with a thief, hateth his own soul: he heareth cursing, and discloseth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.29.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.29.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The fear of man bringeth a snare: but he who putteth his trust in the LORD shall be safe.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.29.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.29.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Many seek the ruler's favor; but ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "every",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " man's judgment ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "cometh",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.29.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.29.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "An unjust man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " an abomination to the just: and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upright in the way ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " abomination to the wicked.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
